    "created_at": "2022-08-09T14:02:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-08-09T14:02:20Z",
    "body": "Do we think that \"sequentially focusable\" will become a confusing term once focusgroup is introduced? The items in a focusgroup are still sequentially focusable, but with the up/down arrow keys.  Apologies for the bikeshedding :)\r\nSince \"tabbable\" is too device-specific, perhaps \"in the primary focus cycle\" ?.",
